# Example requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or the JetBrains HTTP client).
# Everything goes through the API gateway. Send "Login" first; its token is reused below.

@gateway = http://localhost:8000/api
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Gateway health check
GET {{gateway}}

### Login (demo account created by the seed script)
# @name login
POST {{gateway}}/sv_1/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "director@erp.local",
    "password": "admin123"
}

### Current user
GET {{gateway}}/sv_1/current
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List users
GET {{gateway}}/sv_1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List roles
GET {{gateway}}/sv_1/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List stores
GET {{gateway}}/sv_2/stores
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a store
POST {{gateway}}/sv_2/stores
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "name": "New Demo Store",
    "address": "3 Demo Street, Cau Giay, Hanoi",
    "manager_id": "64b000000000000000000101"
}

### Create a category
POST {{gateway}}/sv_3/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Vegetables" }

### List products
GET {{gateway}}/sv_3/products

### List stock items of a store
GET {{gateway}}/sv_3/items/in-store/64b000000000000000000001

### List orders
GET {{gateway}}/sv_4/orders

### Analysis: departments per store (historical data)
GET {{gateway}}/sv_5/analysis/truth/department

### Analysis: run the sales forecast (call this before the other predict endpoints)
GET {{gateway}}/sv_5/run/predict

### Analysis: last year, this year and the 4-week forecast
GET {{gateway}}/sv_5/analysis/predict/weeklySaleInYear
